BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moonlit Mystic Graveyard Ghost Tours
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260304
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
DTSTAMP:20261107T164402Z
UID:87cc9db5307d7b0277c324c812fb@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:There’s nothing more intimately haunting than a colonial bur
 ial ground and Mystic boasts some of the most fascinating and haunted buri
 al grounds around. The Graveyard Ghost tour takes place at Whitehall Buria
 l Ground just off Hendel Drive in Mystic. Whitehall Burial Ground establis
 hed in the 1660’s was one of the common burial places of Mystic until th
 e rural landscape movement arrived to Mystic in 1854. Our Graveyard Ghost 
 Tour tells tales of some of Mystic’s most famous residents.\n\nSource: h
 ttps://ctvisit.com/events/moonlit-mystic-graveyard-ghost-tours-1
LOCATION:Hendel Drive\, Mystic CT\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/moonlit-mystic-graveyard-ghost-tours-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:America250: THE REAL REVOLUTION
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271202
DTSTAMP:20261107T164402Z
UID:d496508c04ff23629e29f741202e@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:A mother with sons on opposing side of a life-changing conflic
 t. Enslaved men risking their lives for freedom. A woman posing as a man i
 n the fight for liberty. These are just a few of the people who are explor
 ed in The Real Revolution\, Westport Museum’s 2026 exhibit honoring the 
 250th anniversary of the founding of the nation. The exhibit delves into t
 he untold stories of the people who lived through the life-changing events
  of war and nation building. The exhibition includes an interactive playro
 om for kids\, and a tavern room in which special events will be held.\n\nS
 ource: https://ctvisit.com/events/america250-real-revolution
LOCATION:Westport Museum For History And Culture\, 25 Avery Place\, Westpo
 rt CT\, 06880
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/america250-real-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Words on Wood Party
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261224
DTSTAMP:20261107T164402Z
UID:30141fc642694de689a557083d0e@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Choose a Words on Wood design or design your own. We will prep
 are all of your materials and when you arrive\, we will walk you through t
 he process\, step by step\, to create your masterpiece. Make sure to check
  out the shops offered at Wallingford Marketplace while you’re here! You
 ’re invited to join us early to shop & take photos in the photo booth. B
 everages – wine\, beer\, cider & soft drinks – are available to purcha
 se at the bar. Outside food is welcome\, but outside beverages are not per
 mitted. Mention CTVisit for a free drink at The Woodshed Bar during the pa
 rty.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/words-wood-party-1
LOCATION:The Wallingford Marketplace at Words on Wood\, 144 CENTER STREET
 \, WALLINGFORD CT\, 06492
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/words-wood-party-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Norwich Stories of the American Revolution
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280101
DTSTAMP:20261107T164402Z
UID:c5d13aef0c36e1820a30a1a8eed9@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Norwich\, Connecticut was a center of Revolutionary activity i
 n Eastern Connecticut. From bands of Sons of Liberty to dedicated soldiers
  of all backgrounds\, the city produced scores of men and women who served
  in all capacities. From humble militiamen to a Signer of the Declaration 
 of Independence\, come and learn the lesser-known stories of these valiant
  Patriots as well as the story of America’s most infamous traitor\, Bene
 dict Arnold.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-america
 n-revolution
LOCATION:Slater Memorial Museum\, 108 Crescent Street\, Norwich CT\, 06360
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-american-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
