DTSTAMP:20261107T164402Z
UID:3a0f441c01737619bb80b1ba710b@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Experience the thrill of horseback riding at our beautiful new
  facility in Woodbury\, CT! Our Fall Riding Programs offer fun\, friendly 
 lessons for riders of all ages and skill levels in a safe and supportive e
 nvironment. Join us in our spacious indoor arena and outdoor ring to build
  new skills\, confidence\, and lasting memories. Choose from three conveni
 ent 5-week sessions running from September through December\, with classes
  every Thursday from 5:00 to 6:00 PM. Spaces fill quickly—sign up today 
 to secure your spot and make it a fall to remember!\n\nSource: https://ctv
 isit.com/events/fall-riding-programs
LOCATION:Barre Equestrian\, 76 Cowles Rd.\, Woodbury CT\, 06798
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/fall-riding-programs
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibition: Stars & Stripes - The American Flag from 9/11 to 250
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
DTSTAMP:20261107T164402Z
UID:2dee3dd24987876baebf5ed4155e@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:2026 marks the momentous occasion of the United States celebra
 ting 250 years as a nation\, and also marks 25 years since the 9/11 terror
 ist attacks. This September\, Slater Memorial Museum of Norwich Free Acade
 my brings to life a display of memories as captured by artist and author R
 obert Carley. Carley’s documentation of post-9/11 America showcases vivi
 d and meaningful images of the American flag across the country\, expresse
 d in dozens of different forms.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/exhi
 bition-stars-stripes-american-flag-911-250
LOCATION:Converse Gallery\, Slater Memorial Museum\, 108 Crescent Street\,
  Norwich CT\, 06360
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/exhibition-stars-stripes-american-flag-911-
 250
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hieroglyphs to Hype: The Modern Afterlife of Ancient Egypt
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260918
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
DTSTAMP:20261107T164402Z
UID:11204f08b00e7472a22ffdd9779c@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Hieroglyphs to Hype: The Modern Afterlife of Ancient Egypt wil
 l explore the enduring fascination with ancient Egyptian art and culture (
 dubbed “Egyptomania” by 19th-century Europeans) through a selection of
  paintings\, prints\, photographs\, and decorative art ranging from the ea
 rly 19th century through the present day. These objects\, from the humble 
 to the refined\, from the shamelessly commercial to the Afrofuturist\, rep
 resent the range of artistic responses to – and misconceptions about –
  ancient Egyptian visual culture.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/hi
 eroglyphs-hype-modern-afterlife-ancient-egypt
LOCATION:Bellarmine Hall\, Bellarmine Hall Galleries\, 1073 N. Benson Road
 \, Fairfield CT\, 06824-3826
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/hieroglyphs-hype-modern-afterlife-ancient-e
 gypt
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
