UID:b81a1acaee14f13fe7689983833b@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Early winter in Connecticut sees an influx of waterfowl specie
 s\, as birds head south to avoid freezing waterways further north. We'll s
 earch for ducks and geese at the mouth of the Connecticut River and in Lon
 g Island Sound\, as well as any late migrants and early winter residents. 
 The walk will be approximately 1-1.5 miles on level paved\, grass\, sandy
 \, and dirt terrain. Exposure to wind\, sun\, and cold possible depending 
 on the weather. No restrooms on site.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/event
 s/waterfowl-walk-1
LOCATION:Fenwick\, 580 Maple Avenue\, Old Saybrook CT\, 06475
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/waterfowl-walk-1
